\section{Noise matrix vs signal matrix}{

This function returns the \strong{noise matrix} (\verb{pixels x pool_size},
the basis patterns from stimulus generation, \emph{input} to CI
computation). The \strong{signal matrix} (\code{\link[=read_signal_matrix]{read_signal_matrix()}}) is a
different object: \verb{pixels x participants}, one column per
producer's CI after base subtraction, \emph{output} of CI computation
and \emph{input} to reliability metrics. Both readers are exported
under \verb{read_*} names and operate independently.
}

\section{What is in an rcicr \code{.RData}}{

\code{load("rcic_stimuli.Rdata")} adds the following objects:
\describe{
\item{\code{base_face_files}}{Named list of file paths to the
original face images. List names are the labels passed
downstream as \code{base_image = "..."}.}
\item{\code{base_faces}}{Base images themselves, loaded as numeric
matrices of grayscale pixels in \verb{[0, 1]}.}
\item{\code{img_size}}{Side length of the (square) images in pixels.}
\item{\code{n_trials}}{Number of stimulus pairs generated.}
\item{\code{p}}{The noise basis. List with \verb{$patches} (sinusoidal
dictionary) and \verb{$patchIdx} (index map).}
\item{\code{stimuli_params}}{Per-trial recipe: list of matrices, one
per base label. Each row is one trial's contrast weights.}
\item{\code{seed}, \code{label}, \code{stimulus_path}, \code{trial},
\code{generator_version}, \code{use_same_parameters}}{Bookkeeping.}
\item{\code{reference_norms}}{Random-responder Frobenius norms,
inserted in place by \code{rcicr::computeInfoVal2IFC()}. Not
present at first.}
}
Trial-level noise images are not stored in the rdata; this
